#: manual/conventions.md:1
msgid "Repository conventions"
msgstr "仓库约定"

#: manual/conventions.md:3
msgid "These rules add to the Luna-Flow documentation standard for `mooncake_impact_factor`. The repository combines three MoonBit packages (`score`, `cli` and `static_search`), a Python index builder, and a Next.js application, so its documentation must keep all of them in step."
msgstr "这些规则是对 Luna-Flow 文档标准针对 `mooncake_impact_factor` 的补充。本仓库包含三个 MoonBit 包（`score`、`cli` 和 `static_search`）、一个 Python 索引构建器和一个 Next.js 应用，因此其文档必须让所有这些部分保持一致。"

#: manual/conventions.md:8
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "范围"

#: manual/conventions.md:10
msgid "Describe the current **`0.1.2`** baseline on the branch."
msgstr "描述当前分支上的 **`0.1.2`** 基线。"

#: manual/conventions.md:11
msgid "Do not document unpublished commands, routes, fields, or MoonBit exports."
msgstr "不要记录尚未发布的命令、路由、字段或 MoonBit 导出。"

#: manual/conventions.md:12
msgid "When behavior is local-only, say so directly instead of implying a global service contract."
msgstr "行为只在本地生效时要直接说明，不要暗示存在全局服务契约。"

#: manual/conventions.md:15
msgid "Consistency"
msgstr "一致性"

#: manual/conventions.md:17
msgid "`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and the manual must tell the same release story."
msgstr "`README.md`、`CONTRIBUTING.md` 和手册必须讲同一个版本故事。"

#: manual/conventions.md:18
msgid "API docs must match the actual MoonBit package name, function signatures, and Next.js route contracts."
msgstr "API 文档必须匹配真实的 MoonBit 包名、函数签名和 Next.js 路由契约。"

#: manual/conventions.md:19
msgid "If Python scripts expose stable CLI flags, database behavior, or search semantics, document them explicitly."
msgstr "如果 Python 脚本暴露了稳定 CLI 参数、数据库行为或搜索语义，要明确写出来。"

#: manual/conventions.md:20
msgid "Distinguish local registry facts from authoritative mooncakes facts."
msgstr "要区分“本地注册表事实”和“mooncakes 权威事实”。"

#: manual/conventions.md:21
msgid "The score formula, rank thresholds and momentum rules are owned by `src/score`. The design page derives their properties from the code; change both in the same commit."
msgstr "分数公式、等级阈值和势头规则归 `src/score` 所有。设计页面根据代码推导它们的性质；两者要在同一个提交中修改。"

#: manual/conventions.md:22
msgid "Behaviour implemented outside MoonBit (signal counting, query evaluation) is documented in the guide or design page that uses it, with a link to the file that implements it."
msgstr "在 MoonBit 之外实现的行为（信号统计、查询求值）记录在使用它的指南或设计页面中，并链接到实现它的文件。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:1
msgid "cli design"
msgstr "cli 设计"

#: manual/design/cli.md:3
msgid "The `cli` package is a bridge: it lets the Python index builder and other non-MoonBit programs evaluate the MoonBit score rules. This page explains the shape of that bridge. The score rules themselves are derived in the [score design](score.md)."
msgstr "`cli` 包是一座桥：它让 Python 索引构建器和其他非 MoonBit 程序能够调用 MoonBit 的评分规则。本页解释这座桥的形态。评分规则本身在 [score 设计](score.md)中推导。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:8
#: manual/design/score.md:9
#: manual/design/static_search.md:18
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr "设计目标"

#: manual/design/cli.md:10
msgid "There must be exactly one implementation of the score, rank and momentum rules, and the database the web application serves must be computed by it. The index builder is written in Python because it works with SQLite, the file system and HTTP; the rules are written in MoonBit so that MoonBit users can call them as a library. The bridge has to connect the two without copying the rules, with as little machinery as possible."
msgstr "分数、等级和势头规则必须只有一份实现，并且 Web 应用提供的数据库必须由它计算。索引构建器用 Python 编写，因为它要处理 SQLite、文件系统和 HTTP；规则用 MoonBit 编写，以便 MoonBit 用户把它们当作库来调用。这座桥必须在不复制规则的前提下，以尽可能少的机制把两者连接起来。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:17
#: manual/design/score.md:18
#: manual/design/static_search.md:25
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr "数学背景"

#: manual/design/cli.md:19
msgid "The command computes a function of eight integers,"
msgstr "该命令计算一个关于八个整数的函数，"

#: manual/design/cli.md:25
msgid "namely `compute_score_snapshot`. Its input arrives as JSON, so the command first applies a total decoding map $d$ from JSON values to $\\mathbb{Z}^8$ and prints $f(d(x))$. For each key $k$,"
msgstr "即 `compute_score_snapshot`。它的输入以 JSON 形式到达，因此命令先应用一个从 JSON 值到 $\\mathbb{Z}^8$ 的全解码映射 $d$，再输出 $f(d(x))$。对每个键 $k$，"

#: manual/design/cli.md:37
msgid "where $\\operatorname{trunc}$ rounds toward zero and $\\operatorname{sat}$ clamps to $[-2^{31}, 2^{31} - 1]$. Because $d$ is total, the only failures are the ones outside it: wrong arguments, an unreadable file and text that is not JSON. Since the score clamps negative counts to $0$, the composite $f \\circ d$ maps every JSON value to a snapshot."
msgstr "其中 $\\operatorname{trunc}$ 向零取整，$\\operatorname{sat}$ 把值截到 $[-2^{31}, 2^{31} - 1]$。由于 $d$ 是全函数，唯一的失败都发生在它之外：参数错误、文件不可读以及文本不是 JSON。又因为评分会把负计数截为 $0$，复合映射 $f \\circ d$ 会把每个 JSON 值映射到一个快照。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:43
msgid "Two properties follow and are what callers rely on:"
msgstr "由此得出两条性质，也是调用方所依赖的："

#: manual/design/cli.md:45
msgid "**Determinism.** $f$ and $d$ are pure, so the same file always gives the same output, byte for byte: `Json::stringify` writes the fields in declaration order and, on the JavaScript target, prints each `Double` in its shortest round-trip form."
msgstr "**确定性。** $f$ 和 $d$ 都是纯函数，因此同一个文件总是逐字节地给出相同输出：`Json::stringify` 按声明顺序写出字段，并且在 JavaScript 目标上以最短往返形式打印每个 `Double`。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:49
msgid "**Agreement with the library.** For an input object with integer values in the `Int` range, $d$ is the identity on those values, so the command prints exactly `Json(@score.compute_score_snapshot(...))`."
msgstr "**与库一致。** 对于值为 `Int` 范围内整数的输入对象，$d$ 在这些值上是恒等映射，因此命令输出的恰好是 `Json(@score.compute_score_snapshot(...))`。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:53
#: manual/design/score.md:165
#: manual/design/static_search.md:146
msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr "设计决策"

#: manual/design/cli.md:55
msgid "A process per snapshot, through a file"
msgstr "每个快照一个进程，通过文件传递"

#: manual/design/cli.md:57
msgid "**Problem.** Python must call MoonBit code."
msgstr "**问题。** Python 必须调用 MoonBit 代码。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:59
msgid "**Options.** Re-implement the formula in Python; call MoonBit compiled to WebAssembly from Python; run a long-lived MoonBit server; run a MoonBit program per snapshot."
msgstr "**选项。** 用 Python 重新实现公式；从 Python 调用编译为 WebAssembly 的 MoonBit；运行一个常驻的 MoonBit 服务器；每个快照运行一次 MoonBit 程序。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:63
msgid "**Choice.** A JavaScript executable that Python starts once per package, with the input in a temporary file. A Python copy of the formula would be a second source of truth (an unused one still exists in `scripts/build_index.py`); a WebAssembly host or a server would add a dependency or a protocol for a job that runs once per index build. The file keeps the command line short and lets the builder delete the input in a `finally` block."
msgstr "**选择。** 一个由 Python 为每个包启动一次的 JavaScript 可执行程序，输入放在临时文件中。Python 版本的公式会成为第二个事实来源（`scripts/build_index.py` 中仍有一份未被使用的副本）；WebAssembly 宿主或服务器会为一个每次构建索引只运行一次的任务增加依赖或协议。使用文件可以让命令行保持简短，也让构建器能在 `finally` 块中删除输入文件。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:70
msgid "The cost is one Node.js start per package. Starting a process takes tens of milliseconds while the score takes microseconds, so the builder's scoring phase is $\\Theta(N)$ process starts for $N$ packages. For a registry of a few thousand packages that is acceptable for an offline build."
msgstr "代价是每个包启动一次 Node.js。启动一个进程需要几十毫秒，而计算分数只需要几微秒，因此对于 $N$ 个包，构建器的评分阶段需要 $\\Theta(N)$ 次进程启动。对于几千个包的注册表，这对离线构建来说是可以接受的。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:75
msgid "JavaScript only"
msgstr "仅限 JavaScript"

#: manual/design/cli.md:77
msgid "The command reads files with `fs.readFileSync` and exits with `process.exit`, both through `extern \"js\"` functions, so the package sets `supported_targets = \"js\"`. The repository needs Node.js anyway for the web application, so no other runtime is required."
msgstr "该命令通过 `extern \"js\"` 函数用 `fs.readFileSync` 读取文件、用 `process.exit` 退出，因此该包设置了 `supported_targets = \"js\"`。仓库的 Web 应用本来就需要 Node.js，所以不需要其他运行时。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:82
msgid "Lenient input, strict errors"
msgstr "宽松输入，严格报错"

#: manual/design/cli.md:84
msgid "**Problem.** A caller may not know every signal, for example the downloads of a package that the builder could not look up."
msgstr "**问题。** 调用方可能并不知道每一个信号，例如构建器未能查到下载量的包。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:87
msgid "**Choice.** Missing and non-numeric fields decode to `0`, the neutral value of every signal. Malformed JSON and bad arguments, which point to a bug in the caller rather than to missing data, produce an `error` object and exit status `1`. The error objects are JSON so that a caller can parse standard output in every case."
msgstr "**选择。** 缺失和非数字的字段解码为 `0`，这是每个信号的中性值。格式错误的 JSON 和错误的参数说明调用方有 bug，而不是数据缺失，因此会产生一个 `error` 对象并以状态 `1` 退出。错误对象采用 JSON 格式，使调用方在任何情况下都能解析标准输出。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:93
msgid "Labels computed in MoonBit"
msgstr "在 MoonBit 中计算标签"

#: manual/design/cli.md:95
msgid "The command returns labels, not only numbers. If the builder computed `rank_label` itself from the stored score, a change of thresholds in MoonBit would silently not reach the database. Returning the whole snapshot keeps the labels and the numbers from one evaluation, so the [snapshot consistency](score.md#snapshot-consistency) invariant holds in the database too."
msgstr "该命令返回标签，而不仅仅是数字。如果构建器根据存储的分数自行计算 `rank_label`，MoonBit 中阈值的修改就会悄无声息地无法反映到数据库中。返回完整快照可以让标签和数字来自同一次求值，因此[快照一致性](score.md#snapshot-consistency)不变量在数据库中同样成立。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:102
#: manual/design/score.md:230
#: manual/design/static_search.md:192
msgid "Correctness / invariants"
msgstr "正确性与不变量"

#: manual/design/cli.md:104
msgid "Exit status `0` implies that standard output is one line containing a JSON object with the seven `ScoreSnapshot` fields."
msgstr "退出状态为 `0` 意味着标准输出是一行包含七个 `ScoreSnapshot` 字段的 JSON 对象。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:106
msgid "Exit status `1` with a JSON object on standard output implies an `error` key. An unreadable input file also exits with `1` but writes only to standard error."
msgstr "退出状态为 `1` 且标准输出为 JSON 对象时，该对象一定带有 `error` 键。无法读取输入文件时也以 `1` 退出，但只向标准错误写入内容。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:109
msgid "The output does not depend on the current time, the environment or any file other than the input: all time-dependent signals are computed by the caller."
msgstr "输出不依赖于当前时间、环境或输入之外的任何文件：所有与时间相关的信号都由调用方计算。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:113
#: manual/design/score.md:306
#: manual/design/static_search.md:245
msgid "Alternatives rejected"
msgstr "被否决的方案"

#: manual/design/cli.md:115
msgid "**Reading standard input.** It would avoid the temporary file, but `readFileSync` on a path works the same on every platform Node.js supports, and the file can be inspected when a build goes wrong."
msgstr "**读取标准输入。** 它可以省去临时文件，但对路径使用 `readFileSync` 在 Node.js 支持的每个平台上行为都相同，而且构建出错时还可以检查该文件。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:118
msgid "**A batch mode** that scores many packages per process would remove the per-package start-up cost. It is not implemented; the per-package contract is simpler and fast enough for the current registry size."
msgstr "**批处理模式**可以在一个进程中为多个包评分，从而省去逐包启动的开销。它尚未实现；逐包的约定更简单，对于当前的注册表规模也足够快。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:121
msgid "**Command-line flags for each signal** (`--dependents 20`) would make the call longer and need a parser; JSON matches the dictionary the builder already has."
msgstr "**为每个信号提供命令行标志**（`--dependents 20`）会让调用变长，还需要解析器；JSON 与构建器已有的字典直接对应。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:125
#: manual/design/score.md:321
#: manual/design/static_search.md:255
msgid "Boundaries"
msgstr "边界"

#: manual/design/cli.md:127
msgid "The command evaluates one snapshot. It does not read the registry, query SQLite, fetch downloads or compute dates."
msgstr "该命令只计算一个快照。它不读取注册表、不查询 SQLite、不获取下载量，也不计算日期。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:129
msgid "It does not validate that the signals are consistent with each other."
msgstr "它不验证信号之间是否一致。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:130
msgid "It reports unreadable files through Node.js, not as JSON."
msgstr "它通过 Node.js 而不是以 JSON 报告不可读的文件。"

#: manual/design/cli.md:131
msgid "It runs only on the JavaScript target with Node.js."
msgstr "它只在 JavaScript 目标上配合 Node.js 运行。"

#: manual/design/score.md:1
msgid "score design"
msgstr "score 设计"

#: manual/design/score.md:3
msgid "This page derives the properties of the scoring model in [`src/score/impact_factor.mbt`](../../../src/score/impact_factor.mbt) and explains why it has this shape. The [score API](../api/score.md) lists the functions; the [architecture guide](../architecture.md) shows where the index builder gets the signals from."
msgstr "本页推导 [`src/score/impact_factor.mbt`](../../../src/score/impact_factor.mbt) 中评分模型的性质，并解释它为何是这种形态。[score API](../api/score.md) 列出了各个函数；[架构指南](../architecture.md)说明索引构建器从哪里获得信号。"

#: manual/design/score.md:11
msgid "The score must order the packages of a registry snapshot by how much the ecosystem relies on them, from signals that a local registry index can provide. It must be cheap, deterministic and explainable: a reader of the web page should be able to see why one package outranks another, and the same signals must give the same score in MoonBit, in the index builder and in the browser."
msgstr "分数必须依据本地注册表索引所能提供的信号，按生态对各包的依赖程度为注册表快照中的包排序。它必须计算廉价、结果确定且可解释：网页的读者应能看出一个包为何排在另一个之前，并且相同的信号在 MoonBit、索引构建器和浏览器中必须给出相同的分数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:20
msgid "The score"
msgstr "分数"

#: manual/design/score.md:22
msgid "Write $D$, $R$ and $W$ for the number of dependents, recent dependents and downloads, and $t$ for the days since the latest release. The implementation computes"
msgstr "记 $D$、$R$、$W$ 分别为依赖方、近期依赖方和下载量，$t$ 为距最新发布的天数。实现计算的是"

#: manual/design/score.md:32
msgid "where $B$ is the base score and $m$ is the step function"
msgstr "其中 $B$ 是基础分，$m$ 是阶梯函数"

#: manual/design/score.md:45
msgid "with negative $t$ treated as $0$. Nothing else enters the score: there is no normalisation against the rest of the registry, so a package's score does not change when other packages are added."
msgstr "负的 $t$ 按 $0$ 处理。除此之外没有任何东西进入分数：不会相对于注册表其余部分做规范化，因此添加其他包时一个包的分数不会改变。"

#: manual/design/score.md:49
msgid "A logarithmic index"
msgstr "对数指数"

#: manual/design/score.md:51
msgid "Because $\\ln a + \\ln b = \\ln ab$, the base score is the logarithm of a weighted product:"
msgstr "因为 $\\ln a + \\ln b = \\ln ab$，基础分是一个加权乘积的对数："

#: manual/design/score.md:61
msgid "The product $(1+D)^{38}(1+R)^{27}(1+W)^{22}$ is a Cobb–Douglas index[^cd] of the shifted counts, and the weights are its elasticities: $\\partial B / \\partial \\ln(1+D) = 38$. Two consequences follow directly."
msgstr "乘积 $(1+D)^{38}(1+R)^{27}(1+W)^{22}$ 是平移后计数的 Cobb–Douglas 指数[^cd]，权重就是它的弹性：$\\partial B / \\partial \\ln(1+D) = 38$。由此直接得出两个推论。"

#: manual/design/score.md:65
msgid "The Cobb–Douglas form $\\prod_i x_i^{\\alpha_i}$ comes from production economics (Cobb and Douglas, 1928). Its logarithm is linear in $\\ln x_i$, which is why ranking by $B$ is the same as ranking by the weighted geometric mean of the shifted counts."
msgstr "Cobb–Douglas 形式 $\\prod_i x_i^{\\alpha_i}$ 源自生产经济学（Cobb 与 Douglas，1928）。它的对数关于 $\\ln x_i$ 是线性的，这就是按 $B$ 排序等同于按平移后计数的加权几何平均排序的原因。"

#: manual/design/score.md:70
msgid "**Doubling adds a constant.** Since $\\sigma(2n+1) = \\ln(2n+2) = \\ln 2 + \\sigma(n)$, doubling $1 + D$ adds $38\\ln 2 \\approx 26.34$ points to $B$, whatever $D$ was. The same step is worth $27\\ln 2 \\approx 18.71$ points for recent dependents and $22\\ln 2 \\approx 15.25$ for downloads. A package with 1000 dependents gains as much from the next 1001 as a package with 10 gains from the next 11."
msgstr "**翻倍增加一个常数。** 由于 $\\sigma(2n+1) = \\ln(2n+2) = \\ln 2 + \\sigma(n)$，把 $1 + D$ 翻倍会让 $B$ 增加 $38\\ln 2 \\approx 26.34$ 分，与 $D$ 原来是多少无关。对近期依赖方，同样一步值 $27\\ln 2 \\approx 18.71$ 分，对下载量值 $22\\ln 2 \\approx 15.25$ 分。拥有 1000 个依赖方的包再获得 1001 个，与拥有 10 个依赖方的包再获得 11 个，收益相同。"

#: manual/design/score.md:77
msgid "**Diminishing returns.** One more dependent adds"
msgstr "**收益递减。** 多一个依赖方会增加"

#: manual/design/score.md:84
msgid "using $\\ln(1+x) \\le x$ with $x = 1/(D+1)$. The marginal value of a dependent falls like $1/D$. Inflating one count therefore buys little: multiplying $1 + W$ by ten adds exactly $22 \\ln 10 \\approx 50.66$ points to $B$, whatever $W$ was, which is less than the distance between any two neighbouring rank thresholds ($60$, $70$ and $80$ points)."
msgstr "这里用到了 $\\ln(1+x) \\le x$，取 $x = 1/(D+1)$。一个依赖方的边际价值按 $1/D$ 递减。因此单独抬高一个计数收效甚微：把 $1 + W$ 乘以十，无论 $W$ 原来是多少，都恰好给 $B$ 增加 $22 \\ln 10 \\approx 50.66$ 分，小于任意两个相邻等级阈值之间的距离（$60$、$70$ 和 $80$ 分）。"

#: manual/design/score.md:90
msgid "Rank thresholds as counts"
msgstr "以计数表示的等级阈值"

#: manual/design/score.md:92
msgid "The rank buckets are thresholds on $S$: `S` from $260$, `A` from $180$, `B` from $110$, `C` from $50$. Inverting $\\sigma$ shows what they mean in counts. With $m = 1$ and a single non-zero signal of weight $w$, the score reaches a threshold $T$ when"
msgstr "等级桶是 $S$ 上的阈值：`S` 从 $260$ 起，`A` 从 $180$ 起，`B` 从 $110$ 起，`C` 从 $50$ 起。对 $\\sigma$ 求逆即可看出它们对应的计数。当 $m = 1$ 且只有一个权重为 $w$ 的非零信号时，分数在以下条件下达到阈值 $T$"

#: manual/design/score.md:102
msgid "so the smallest integer count is $\\lceil e^{T/w} - 1 \\rceil$:"
msgstr "所以最小的整数计数是 $\\lceil e^{T/w} - 1 \\rceil$："

#: manual/design/score.md:104
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "阈值"

#: manual/design/score.md:104
msgid "Dependents only ($w = 38$)"
msgstr "仅依赖方（$w = 38$）"

#: manual/design/score.md:104
msgid "Recent dependents only ($w = 27$)"
msgstr "仅近期依赖方（$w = 27$）"

#: manual/design/score.md:104
msgid "Downloads only ($w = 22$)"
msgstr "仅下载量（$w = 22$）"

#: manual/design/score.md:111
msgid "For example $38\\ln 937 \\approx 260.02$ while $38\\ln 936 \\approx 259.98$, so 936 dependents are the first count to reach `S` on their own. In practice the signals combine: 20 dependents, 4 recent dependents and 300 downloads already give $B \\approx 284.7$."
msgstr "例如 $38\\ln 937 \\approx 260.02$，而 $38\\ln 936 \\approx 259.98$，所以 936 是单凭依赖方就能达到 `S` 的最小计数。实际中各信号会叠加：20 个依赖方、4 个近期依赖方和 300 次下载已能得到 $B \\approx 284.7$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:116
msgid "Growth and momentum"
msgstr "增长与势头"

#: manual/design/score.md:118
msgid "A snapshot evaluates the score twice, on the current signals and on the signals of 30 days ago, and defines"
msgstr "快照对分数求值两次，一次基于当前信号，一次基于 30 天前的信号，并定义"

#: manual/design/score.md:131
msgid "Since $m(t) > 0$ and every term of $B$ is non-negative, $S_{30} = 0$ exactly when every historical count is $0$ (or negative, which clamps to $0$): the package had no dependents and no downloads 30 days ago. Otherwise at least one $\\sigma$ is at least $\\sigma(1) = \\ln 2$, so"
msgstr "由于 $m(t) > 0$ 且 $B$ 的每一项都非负，$S_{30} = 0$ 当且仅当所有历史计数都为 $0$（或为负，负值会被截断为 $0$）：该包在 30 天前既没有依赖方，也没有下载量。否则至少有一个 $\\sigma$ 不小于 $\\sigma(1) = \\ln 2$，因此"

#: manual/design/score.md:140
msgid "the smallest weight times the smallest multiplier. The score therefore takes no values in $(0, 13.42)$, and $G / S_{30}$ is never divided by a tiny denominator. For $S_{30} = 0$ the relative growth is undefined, and the implementation uses $1$ (that is, 100 %) instead of $+\\infty$ so that $r$ stays finite and can be stored and sorted. A new package with $S \\ge 35$ and three recent dependents is therefore `Rising`."
msgstr "即最小权重乘以最小乘数。因此分数不会取 $(0, 13.42)$ 中的值，$G / S_{30}$ 永远不会除以很小的分母。当 $S_{30} = 0$ 时，相对增长没有定义，实现用 $1$（即 100 %）代替 $+\\infty$，使 $r$ 保持有限，便于存储和排序。因此，一个 $S \\ge 35$ 且有三个最近依赖方的新包会被标为 `Rising`。"

#: manual/design/score.md:147
msgid "The momentum label tests three conditions at two levels:"
msgstr "势头标签在两个层级上检验三个条件："

#: manual/design/score.md:154
msgid "The `Rising` conditions imply the `Hot` conditions, so the classes are nested levels of one scale rather than independent tags. When $S_{30} > 0$, $r \\ge \\rho$ is the same as $S \\ge (1 + \\rho) S_{30}$, so `Rising` asks for a score at least $1.35$ times the old one *and* an absolute gain of $35$ points. Each bound covers a case the other misses. The absolute bound stops small packages from rising on a small change: a package that goes from one download to three ($S$ from about $15.2$ to $30.5$ with $m = 1$) doubles its score, $r = 1$, but gains only about $15$ points. The relative bound stops large packages from rising through the noise of a big base: at $S_{30} = 1000$, a gain of $35$ points is $r = 0.035$."
msgstr "`Rising` 的条件蕴含 `Hot` 的条件，因此这些类别是同一刻度上嵌套的层级，而不是相互独立的标记。当 $S_{30} > 0$ 时，$r \\ge \\rho$ 等价于 $S \\ge (1 + \\rho) S_{30}$，所以 `Rising` 要求分数至少是旧分数的 $1.35$ 倍，*并且*绝对增长 $35$ 分。两个下限各自覆盖了对方漏掉的情形。绝对下限防止小包因很小的变化而上升：一个包的下载量从一次变为三次（$m = 1$ 时 $S$ 从约 $15.2$ 变为 $30.5$），分数翻倍，$r = 1$，但只增长约 $15$ 分。相对下限防止大包仅凭庞大基数上的噪声就上升：在 $S_{30} = 1000$ 时，增长 $35$ 分只是 $r = 0.035$。"

#: manual/design/score.md:167
msgid "Logarithms of counts"
msgstr "对计数取对数"

#: manual/design/score.md:169
msgid "**Problem.** Dependent and download counts are heavy-tailed: a few packages have thousands, most have none. A linear score would make the ranking a leaderboard of the largest package in each signal."
msgstr "**问题。** 依赖方数量和下载量呈重尾分布：少数包有成千上万，大多数包一个也没有。线性分数会让排名变成各信号中最大包的排行榜。"

#: manual/design/score.md:173
msgid "**Options.** Raw counts; ranks or percentiles within the registry; square roots; logarithms."
msgstr "**选项。** 原始计数；注册表内的名次或百分位；平方根；对数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:176
msgid "**Choice.** $\\ln(1 + n)$. The shift by one keeps $\\sigma(0) = 0$ finite and makes $S = 0$ exactly when a package has no signal at all. Percentiles would need the whole registry and change a package's score when other packages appear, which breaks the CLI's one-package-at-a-time contract. Square roots still grow without the scale invariance derived above."
msgstr "**选择。** $\\ln(1 + n)$。平移 1 让 $\\sigma(0) = 0$ 保持有限，并使 $S = 0$ 恰好对应一个包完全没有信号的情况。百分位需要整个注册表，并会在出现其他包时改变一个包的分数，从而破坏 CLI 一次一个包的约定。平方根仍然会增长，却没有上面推导出的尺度不变性。"

#: manual/design/score.md:182
msgid "Additive weights"
msgstr "加性权重"

#: manual/design/score.md:184
msgid "**Problem.** The three signals must be combined into one number."
msgstr "**问题。** 三个信号必须合并成一个数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:186
msgid "**Choice.** A weighted sum of logarithms with weights $38 : 27 : 22$. Total dependents capture established adoption and weigh most. Downloads are an external popularity hint that is missing for packages the builder could not look up, so they weigh least. Recent dependents are counted *on top of* total dependents, so a dependent from the recent window contributes to both terms: the recent term is a bonus for current adoption, not a separate population. The weights are editorial choices of this project, not fitted parameters."
msgstr "**选择。** 以 $38 : 27 : 22$ 为权重的对数加权和。依赖方总数反映已经确立的采用度，权重最大。下载量是外部的流行度提示，对于构建器查不到的包会缺失，因此权重最小。近期依赖方是在依赖方总数*之上*额外计数的，所以近期窗口中的一个依赖方会同时贡献两项：近期项是对当前采用的奖励，而不是另一个独立的群体。这些权重是本项目的编辑性选择，而不是拟合得到的参数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:194
msgid "A recency multiplier, not a recency term"
msgstr "用时效乘数而非时效项"

#: manual/design/score.md:196
msgid "**Problem.** Old, unmaintained packages should not hold their rank forever, but age must not outweigh adoption."
msgstr "**问题。** 老旧、无人维护的包不应永远保持其等级，但年龄不能压过采用度。"

#: manual/design/score.md:199
msgid "**Choice.** A multiplicative step function between $0.88$ and $1.12$. Because it multiplies $B$, it changes the score by at most $\\pm 12\\,\\%$, and the ratio between the freshest and the oldest package with the same signals is $1.12 / 0.88 \\approx 1.27$. That can move a package across one rank boundary (for example $B = 240$ gives `S` at $1.12$ and `A` at $0.88$), but never across two: the scores $m(t)\\,B$ of one package lie in $[0.88\\,B,\\ 1.12\\,B]$, an interval whose ends differ by the factor $1.27$, while neighbouring thresholds differ by at least $260 / 180 \\approx 1.44$ ($180 / 110 \\approx 1.64$, $110 / 50 = 2.2$), so the interval contains at most one threshold. Nor does it turn an unused package into a ranked one: $B = 0$ stays $0$. An additive age term would give unused but freshly released packages a positive score."
msgstr "**选择。** 一个介于 $0.88$ 与 $1.12$ 之间的乘性阶梯函数。因为它乘在 $B$ 上，最多使分数变化 $\\pm 12\\,\\%$，信号相同时最新与最旧的包之间的比值为 $1.12 / 0.88 \\approx 1.27$。这可以让一个包跨过一个等级边界（例如 $B = 240$ 在 $1.12$ 时为 `S`，在 $0.88$ 时为 `A`），但不会跨过两个：同一个包的分数 $m(t)\\,B$ 落在 $[0.88\\,B,\\ 1.12\\,B]$ 中，这个区间两端相差 $1.27$ 倍，而相邻阈值至少相差 $260 / 180 \\approx 1.44$ 倍（$180 / 110 \\approx 1.64$，$110 / 50 = 2.2$），所以该区间至多包含一个阈值。它也不会把无人使用的包变成有等级的包：$B = 0$ 仍然是 $0$。加性的年龄项则会给无人使用但刚发布的包一个正分。"

#: manual/design/score.md:212
msgid "Fixed thresholds for labels"
msgstr "标签使用固定阈值"

#: manual/design/score.md:214
msgid "**Problem.** The web pages need short, stable labels."
msgstr "**问题。** 网页需要简短、稳定的标签。"

#: manual/design/score.md:216
msgid "**Choice.** Constant thresholds on $S$ and $G$. Labels therefore mean the same in every snapshot and need no registry-wide statistics. Quantile buckets (\"top 5 %\") would need the whole registry, like percentile scores."
msgstr "**选择。** 在 $S$ 和 $G$ 上使用常数阈值。因此标签在每个快照中含义相同，也不需要全注册表的统计量。分位数桶（\"前 5 %\"）和百分位分数一样，需要整个注册表。"

#: manual/design/score.md:220
msgid "Integers in, `Double` out"
msgstr "整数输入，`Double` 输出"

#: manual/design/score.md:222
msgid "**Problem.** The signals are counts, but the score is real-valued."
msgstr "**问题。** 信号是计数，而分数是实数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:224
msgid "**Choice.** All inputs are `Int`, and negative values are clamped instead of rejected, so every function is total and can be called on raw database values. The scoring functions never abort and return no `Result`; the only non-finite output is the overflow described under [numerical accuracy](#numerical-accuracy)."
msgstr "**选择。** 所有输入都是 `Int`，负值被截断而不是拒绝，因此每个函数都是全函数，可以直接作用于数据库中的原始值。评分函数从不中止，也不返回 `Result`；唯一的非有限输出是[数值精度](#numerical-accuracy)中描述的溢出。"

#: manual/design/score.md:232
msgid "Monotonicity"
msgstr "单调性"

#: manual/design/score.md:234
msgid "For counts in $[0, 2^{31} - 2]$, $S$ is non-decreasing in $D$, $R$ and $W$, and strictly increasing as long as the count stays below $2^{24}$: $\\sigma$ is strictly increasing, the weights are positive and $m(t) > 0$, so"
msgstr "对于 $[0, 2^{31} - 2]$ 内的计数，$S$ 关于 $D$、$R$ 和 $W$ 单调不减，并且只要计数保持在 $2^{24}$ 以下就严格递增：$\\sigma$ 严格递增，权重为正，且 $m(t) > 0$，因此"

#: manual/design/score.md:242
msgid "Above $2^{24}$ the conversion through `Float` (below) can map neighbouring counts to the same value, so strict growth degrades to non-decreasing. $S$ is non-increasing in $t$ because $m$ is. The blackbox tests in `impact_factor_test.mbt` check instances of this for dependents, downloads and release age."
msgstr "超过 $2^{24}$ 后，经由 `Float` 的转换（见下文）可能把相邻计数映射到同一个值，严格递增因此退化为单调不减。$S$ 关于 $t$ 单调不增，因为 $m$ 如此。`impact_factor_test.mbt` 中的黑盒测试针对依赖方、下载量和发布年龄检查了这一性质的实例。"

#: manual/design/score.md:248
msgid "Range"
msgstr "取值范围"

#: manual/design/score.md:250
msgid "$S \\ge 0$, with equality exactly when $D, R, W \\le 0$. For counts up to $2^{31} - 2$, $\\sigma \\le \\ln 2^{31} \\approx 21.49$, so"
msgstr "$S \\ge 0$，且当且仅当 $D, R, W \\le 0$ 时取等号。对于不超过 $2^{31} - 2$ 的计数，$\\sigma \\le \\ln 2^{31} \\approx 21.49$，因此"

#: manual/design/score.md:257
msgid "Labels are total"
msgstr "标签是全函数"

#: manual/design/score.md:259
msgid "`rank_label` and `compute_momentum_label` return one of their labels for every input. Every comparison with `NaN` is false, so a `NaN` score is ranked `D` and has `Stable` momentum."
msgstr "`rank_label` 和 `compute_momentum_label` 对每个输入都返回它们的某个标签。与 `NaN` 的任何比较都为假，所以 `NaN` 分数的等级为 `D`，势头为 `Stable`。"

#: manual/design/score.md:263
msgid "Numerical accuracy"
msgstr "数值精度"

#: manual/design/score.md:265
msgid "`log_signal` converts $n + 1$ to `Float` before taking the logarithm in `Double`. Every integer up to $2^{24}$ is exact in `Float`; above it the conversion rounds to nearest with relative error $|\\delta| \\le u = 2^{-24}$. Then"
msgstr "`log_signal` 先把 $n + 1$ 转换为 `Float`，再在 `Double` 中取对数。不超过 $2^{24}$ 的每个整数在 `Float` 中都是精确的；超过之后，转换按就近舍入，相对误差为 $|\\delta| \\le u = 2^{-24}$。于是"

#: manual/design/score.md:278
msgid "and the error in $S$ from this conversion is at most $1.12 \\cdot 87 \\cdot u/(1-u) \\approx 5.8 \\times 10^{-6}$, on top of the ordinary `Double` rounding of a few operations. The index builder still contains an unused Python copy of the formula (`compute_score` in `scripts/build_index.py`) that calls `math.log1p` without the `Float` step; it agrees with the MoonBit result to this bound plus a few units in the last place. The database itself is filled through the MoonBit CLI."
msgstr "这一转换在 $S$ 中造成的误差至多为 $1.12 \\cdot 87 \\cdot u/(1-u) \\approx 5.8 \\times 10^{-6}$，此外还有几次运算中普通的 `Double` 舍入误差。索引构建器中仍有一份未被使用的 Python 公式副本（`scripts/build_index.py` 中的 `compute_score`），它调用 `math.log1p` 而没有经过 `Float`；它与 MoonBit 结果的差距在上述界限再加上末位几个单位以内。数据库本身是通过 MoonBit CLI 填充的。"

#: manual/design/score.md:286
msgid "The addition $n + 1$ is done in `Int`. For $n = 2^{31} - 1$ it wraps to $-2^{31}$, the logarithm of a negative number is `NaN`, and the score is `NaN`."
msgstr "加法 $n + 1$ 在 `Int` 中进行。当 $n = 2^{31} - 1$ 时它会回绕为 $-2^{31}$，负数的对数是 `NaN`，于是分数为 `NaN`。"

#: manual/design/score.md:290
msgid "Snapshot consistency"
msgstr "快照一致性"

#: manual/design/score.md:292
msgid "`compute_score_snapshot` computes every field from the same two calls of `compute_score`, so `score_growth_30d == score - score_30d_ago` holds exactly (it is the same floating-point subtraction), and `rank_label` and `momentum_label` are always the labels of the stored numbers."
msgstr "`compute_score_snapshot` 的每个字段都来自同样的两次 `compute_score` 调用，所以 `score_growth_30d == score - score_30d_ago` 严格成立（这就是同一次浮点减法），并且 `rank_label` 与 `momentum_label` 始终是所存数值对应的标签。"

#: manual/design/score.md:297
msgid "How scores are ranked"
msgstr "分数如何排序"

#: manual/design/score.md:299
msgid "The package only computes scores; consumers sort them. Every ordering in the repository breaks ties deterministically: the ranked feeds and the default search order use `score` descending, then `full_name` ascending, and the `Hot` and `Rising` feeds use `score_growth_30d` descending, then `score`, then `full_name`. The [static_search design](static_search.md) gives the orderings of the browser search."
msgstr "本包只计算分数，由使用方进行排序。仓库中的每种排序都以确定的方式处理并列：排名 feed 和默认搜索顺序先按 `score` 降序，再按 `full_name` 升序；`Hot` 和 `Rising` feed 先按 `score_growth_30d` 降序，再按 `score`，最后按 `full_name`。浏览器搜索的排序见 [static_search 设计](static_search.md)。"

#: manual/design/score.md:308
msgid "**PageRank-style centrality** on the dependency graph would reward being depended on by important packages, but it needs the whole graph, an iterative solver and a damping parameter, and it cannot be explained on a package page. The direct dependent count is the first step of that iteration and is enough for a registry of this size."
msgstr "依赖图上的 **PageRank 式中心性**会奖励被重要包依赖的包，但它需要整张图、迭代求解器和阻尼参数，而且无法在包页面上解释清楚。直接依赖方计数是该迭代的第一步，对这种规模的注册表已经足够。"

#: manual/design/score.md:313
msgid "**Transitive dependents** were not used: they count the same downstream package many times through every path and favour low-level packages even more than the logarithm can correct."
msgstr "**传递依赖方**没有被采用：它们会沿每条路径把同一个下游包计算多次，比对数所能修正的更偏向底层包。"

#: manual/design/score.md:316
msgid "**Learning the weights** from a labelled ranking would need labels that do not exist; the fixed weights are stated in the code and in this page."
msgstr "**从带标注的排名中学习权重**需要并不存在的标注；固定权重写在代码和本页中。"

#: manual/design/score.md:318
msgid "**Returning `Result` for negative inputs** would push error handling into every caller for a condition that has an obvious meaning (no signal)."
msgstr "**对负输入返回 `Result`** 会把错误处理推给每个调用方，而这种情况本有显而易见的含义（没有信号）。"

#: manual/design/score.md:323
msgid "The score measures adoption inside one registry snapshot. It does not measure code quality, correctness, security or maintenance effort."
msgstr "分数衡量的是单个注册表快照内的采用度。它不衡量代码质量、正确性、安全性或维护投入。"

#: manual/design/score.md:325
msgid "The package takes the signals as given. Collecting them, deciding which dependents are recent and which downloads are trusted is the index builder's job, described in the [architecture guide](../architecture.md)."
msgstr "本包按原样接收信号。收集信号、判定哪些依赖方算近期以及哪些下载量可信，是索引构建器的工作，见[架构指南](../architecture.md)。"

#: manual/design/score.md:328
msgid "The builder currently passes `0` as the historical download count, so `score_growth_30d` contains the whole download term $22\\,m(t)\\,\\sigma(W)$ of the current score. Read growth together with the dependent counts, which the momentum label does by requiring recent dependents."
msgstr "构建器目前把历史下载量传为 `0`，因此 `score_growth_30d` 包含了当前分数中完整的下载项 $22\\,m(t)\\,\\sigma(W)$。请把增长与依赖方计数一起解读，势头标签正是通过要求近期依赖方做到这一点的。"

#: manual/design/score.md:333
msgid "There is no normalisation across packages, no time decay inside a window and no confidence interval: a score is a deterministic function of four integers."
msgstr "不存在跨包的规范化，不存在窗口内的时间衰减，也不存在置信区间：分数是四个整数的确定性函数。"

#: manual/design/score.md:336
msgid "Counts of `2147483647` are not supported (the score becomes `NaN`)."
msgstr "不支持值为 `2147483647` 的计数（分数会变为 `NaN`）。"

#: manual/design/score.md:337
msgid "The builder passes `0` as the historical days since release when the release date is unknown, while the current value is `3650`; such packages get the multiplier $1.12$ 30 days ago and $0.88$ now, which shows as negative growth. The [architecture guide](../architecture.md) gives the signal definitions."
msgstr "当发布日期未知时，构建器把历史发布天数传为 `0`，而当前值为 `3650`；这类包在 30 天前得到乘数 $1.12$，现在得到 $0.88$，表现为负增长。[架构指南](../architecture.md)给出了信号的定义。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:1
msgid "static_search design"
msgstr "static_search 设计"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:3
msgid "The static publishing mode serves the whole application as files, without a server or SQLite. Search then runs in the browser over a precomputed index. This page describes that index and its query algorithm, derives what the ranking means and what it costs, and explains the role of the MoonBit `static_search` package in it. The [static_search API](../api/static_search.md) lists the MoonBit functions."
msgstr "静态发布模式把整个应用作为文件提供，不需要服务器或 SQLite。此时搜索在浏览器中基于预先计算的索引运行。本页描述该索引及其查询算法，推导排名的含义和代价，并解释 MoonBit `static_search` 包在其中的角色。[static_search API](../api/static_search.md) 列出了 MoonBit 函数。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:10
msgid "Three pieces work together:"
msgstr "三个部分协同工作："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:12
msgid "Piece"
msgstr "部分"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:14
msgid "Version tag and lower-case normalisation."
msgstr "版本标记和小写规范化。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:15
msgid "Writes the index and the other static files from the SQLite database."
msgstr "从 SQLite 数据库写出索引和其他静态文件。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:16
msgid "Loads the index into a Web Worker and answers queries."
msgstr "把索引加载到 Web Worker 中并回答查询。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:20
msgid "Search on the static site must accept the same query forms as the dynamic site (the native expression language, the serialised query AST and the simple form fields), stay responsive while the page renders, and need nothing but files that a static host such as GitHub Pages can serve."
msgstr "静态站点上的搜索必须接受与动态站点相同的查询形式（原生表达式语言、序列化的查询 AST 和简单表单字段），在页面渲染时保持响应，并且只需要 GitHub Pages 这类静态托管能提供的文件。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:27
msgid "Data layout"
msgstr "数据布局"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:29
msgid "`export_static_json.py` writes these files under `public/data/`:"
msgstr "`export_static_json.py` 在 `public/data/` 下写出以下文件："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:31
msgid "File"
msgstr "文件"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:31
msgid "Content"
msgstr "内容"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:33
msgid "`schema_version`, `generated_at`, `package_count`, `data_mode = \"static\"` and the size of each feed."
msgstr "`schema_version`、`generated_at`、`package_count`、`data_mode = \"static\"` 以及每个 feed 的大小。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:34
msgid "The three feeds, precomputed with the SQL orderings of the dynamic site."
msgstr "三个 feed，按动态站点的 SQL 排序预先计算。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:35
msgid "The search index: `{ \"items\": [...] }`, one record per package."
msgstr "搜索索引：`{ \"items\": [...] }`，每个包一条记录。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:36
msgid "The same packages with display fields (keywords, version count, multiplier)."
msgstr "同样的包，附带展示用字段（关键词、版本数、乘数）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:37
msgid "Detail page data: package, last 20 versions, dependents."
msgstr "详情页数据：包、最近 20 个版本、依赖方。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:39
msgid "A record of the search index is a flat object. Besides the display fields of a package summary (name, owner, description, version, counts and the score snapshot fields) it holds precomputed search keys:"
msgstr "搜索索引的记录是一个扁平对象。除了包摘要的展示字段（名称、所有者、描述、版本、各计数和分数快照字段）之外，它还保存预先计算的搜索键："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:43
msgid "Value"
msgstr "值"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:45
msgid "The field, trimmed and lower-cased (`\"\"` when missing)."
msgstr "该字段去除首尾空白并转为小写（缺失时为 `\"\"`）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:46
msgid "Each keyword, trimmed and lower-cased."
msgstr "每个关键词，去除首尾空白并转为小写。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:47
msgid "The non-empty parts of full name, owner, package name, description and keywords, joined by single spaces."
msgstr "完整名称、所有者、包名、描述和关键词中非空的部分，用单个空格连接。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:48
msgid "Whether the trimmed field is non-empty."
msgstr "去除首尾空白后该字段是否非空。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:49
msgid "The release timestamp; its first four characters give the year."
msgstr "发布时间戳；其前四个字符给出年份。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:51
msgid "So the index is a *forward* index: an array of $N$ records with $F$ fixed fields each, sorted by `full_name`. There is no inverted index and no tokenisation. Lower-casing at export time means that a query only has to normalise the needle, not every record, at query time."
msgstr "所以该索引是一个*正排*索引：由 $N$ 条记录组成的数组，每条记录有 $F$ 个固定字段，按 `full_name` 排序。没有倒排索引，也没有分词。在导出时转为小写，意味着查询时只需规范化查询词，而不必规范化每条记录。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:56
msgid "Queries as Boolean formulas"
msgstr "作为布尔公式的查询"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:58
msgid "Every query is first turned into a query AST by `deriveQueryAst` in [`lib/query.ts`](../../../lib/query.ts), with this precedence: a serialised `ast` parameter, else a native `expr`, else the legacy form fields joined by AND. An AST is a formula over term predicates:"
msgstr "每个查询都会先由 [`lib/query.ts`](../../../lib/query.ts) 中的 `deriveQueryAst` 转换成查询 AST，优先级如下：序列化的 `ast` 参数，否则是原生 `expr`，否则是用 AND 连接的旧式表单字段。AST 是关于项谓词的公式："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:67
msgid "and a term $t = (f, \\mathit{op}, v)$ is evaluated on a record $p$ as"
msgstr "一个项 $t = (f, \\mathit{op}, v)$ 在记录 $p$ 上的求值为"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:69
msgid "Field $f$"
msgstr "字段 $f$"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:69
msgid "$p \\models t$ when"
msgstr "$p \\models t$ 的条件"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:71
msgid ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ is a substring of the normalised field ($\\n"
"u$ = trim and lower-case); an empty needle always matches."
msgstr ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ 是规范化字段的子串（$\\n"
"u$ = 去除首尾空白并转小写）；空查询词总是匹配。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:72
msgid ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ is a substring of at least one normalised keyword."
msgstr ""
"$\\n"
"u(v)$ 是至少一个规范化关键词的子串。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:73
msgid "the label equals $v$ exactly."
msgstr "标签与 $v$ 完全相等。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:74
msgid "$x \\ge v$ for `>=`, $x \\le v$ for `<=`, $x = v$ otherwise, with $v$ converted by JavaScript `Number`; false when the conversion is not finite. An empty $v$ converts to $0$."
msgstr "`>=` 时为 $x \\ge v$，`<=` 时为 $x \\le v$，其他情况为 $x = v$，其中 $v$ 用 JavaScript 的 `Number` 转换；转换结果不是有限数时为假。空的 $v$ 转换为 $0$。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:75
msgid "the flag equals `v == \"true\"`."
msgstr "标志等于 `v == \"true\"`。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:77
msgid "The result set is $\\{\\, p : p \\models \\varphi \\,\\}$, evaluated recursively with short-circuiting `every` and `some`. An AST without any non-empty term matches every record."
msgstr "结果集为 $\\{\\, p : p \\models \\varphi \\,\\}$，通过短路的 `every` 和 `some` 递归求值。不含任何非空项的 AST 匹配所有记录。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:81
msgid "Relevance"
msgstr "相关度"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:83
msgid "When there is a query and no explicit sort, the worker orders results by a relevance count. With $L(\\varphi)$ the multiset of term leaves of the AST,"
msgstr "当有查询且没有显式指定排序时，worker 按相关度计数排列结果。记 $L(\\varphi)$ 为 AST 的项叶子构成的多重集，"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:90
msgid "where negations are ignored: a leaf under `NOT` counts when its *un-negated* term matches. Ties are broken by score (descending) and then by `full_name` (ascending, by `localeCompare`)."
msgstr "其中忽略否定：`NOT` 之下的叶子在其*未取反*的项匹配时计数。并列时先按分数（降序），再按 `full_name`（升序，使用 `localeCompare`）排序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:94
msgid "Two consequences are worth deriving because they explain what users see."
msgstr "有两个推论值得推导，因为它们解释了用户看到的结果。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:96
msgid "**Conjunctions do not reorder.** Let $\\varphi = t_1 \\land \\dots \\land t_k$ with positive terms. Every result satisfies every $t_i$, so $\\operatorname{rel}(p) = k$ for all results, and the order is exactly the score order. Relevance only has an effect when the formula contains `OR` or `NOT`."
msgstr "**合取不会改变顺序。** 设 $\\varphi = t_1 \\land \\dots \\land t_k$，其中各项都为正项。每个结果都满足所有 $t_i$，所以对所有结果 $\\operatorname{rel}(p) = k$，顺序就是分数顺序。只有当公式含有 `OR` 或 `NOT` 时相关度才起作用。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:102
msgid "**Disjunctions rank by coverage.** For $\\varphi = t_1 \\lor \\dots \\lor t_k$ with positive terms, $\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ is the number of alternatives that $p$ satisfies, so a package that matches every alternative comes first."
msgstr "**析取按覆盖度排序。** 对于由正项构成的 $\\varphi = t_1 \\lor \\dots \\lor t_k$，$\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ 是 $p$ 满足的备选项个数，所以匹配所有备选项的包排在最前。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:106
msgid "**Negated leaves count against the user.** A negated leaf $\\lnot t$ contributes $1$ to $\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ exactly when $p \\models t$, the case the user wanted to exclude. When $\\lnot t$ must hold for every result, for example as a conjunct of the root, no result satisfies $t$ and the leaf contributes $0$ to all of them, so the order is unaffected. Under a disjunction it is not: for $\\varphi = \\lnot t_1 \\lor t_2$,"
msgstr "**取反的叶子反而加分。** 取反的叶子 $\\lnot t$ 恰在 $p \\models t$ 时为 $\\operatorname{rel}(p)$ 贡献 $1$，而这正是用户想排除的情形。当 $\\lnot t$ 必须对每个结果成立时（例如作为根节点的一个合取项），没有结果满足 $t$，该叶子对所有结果贡献 $0$，顺序不受影响。在析取之下则不然：对于 $\\varphi = \\lnot t_1 \\lor t_2$，"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:117
msgid "so a result that satisfies both $t_1$ and $t_2$ (relevance $2$) comes before one that satisfies only $t_2$ (relevance $1$), and results that satisfy neither (relevance $0$) come last, although $\\lnot t_1$ holds for them. The same applies to every leaf below a negated group."
msgstr "因此同时满足 $t_1$ 和 $t_2$ 的结果（相关度 $2$）排在只满足 $t_2$ 的结果（相关度 $1$）之前，而两者都不满足的结果（相关度 $0$）排在最后，尽管 $\\lnot t_1$ 对它们成立。取反分组之下的每个叶子也是如此。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:122
msgid "Relevance is therefore a coordination-level match[^coord], not a text statistic: it ignores term frequency, field length and how rare a term is."
msgstr "因此相关度是一种协调级匹配[^coord]，而不是文本统计量：它忽略词频、字段长度以及词的稀有程度。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:125
msgid "Coordination-level matching ranks documents by the number of query terms they contain; it is the simplest ranked retrieval model and predates tf–idf weighting (Salton and McGill, *Introduction to Modern Information Retrieval*, 1983)."
msgstr "协调级匹配按文档包含的查询词数量为文档排序；它是最简单的排序检索模型，早于 tf–idf 加权（Salton 与 McGill，*Introduction to Modern Information Retrieval*，1983）。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:130
msgid "Sort orders and tie-breaking"
msgstr "排序方式与并列处理"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:132
msgid "The other sort keys are `score`, `growth`, `downloads`, `dependents`, `recent`, `updated` (the release year) and `name`. Each comparison is"
msgstr "其他排序键为 `score`、`growth`、`downloads`、`dependents`、`recent`、`updated`（发布年份）和 `name`。每次比较为"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:139
msgid "where $x \\Vert y$ means \"$x$ if non-zero, else $y$\" and $s = -1$ for descending, $+1$ for ascending order. The default order is ascending for `name` and descending for the other keys. Because $s$ multiplies the whole expression, a descending sort also reverses the name order of ties. Full names are unique, so ties are always resolved and the same index and query give the same order."
msgstr "其中 $x \\Vert y$ 表示\"$x$ 非零时取 $x$，否则取 $y$\"，降序时 $s = -1$，升序时 $s = +1$。`name` 默认升序，其他键默认降序。由于 $s$ 乘在整个表达式上，降序排序也会反转并列项的名称顺序。完整名称是唯一的，因此并列总能被打破，同样的索引和查询总是给出同样的顺序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:148
msgid "Scan a forward index instead of building an inverted one"
msgstr "扫描正排索引，而不是构建倒排索引"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:150
msgid "**Problem.** The browser needs to answer substring, numeric and Boolean queries without a database."
msgstr "**问题。** 浏览器需要在没有数据库的情况下回答子串、数值和布尔查询。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:153
msgid "**Options.** Ship SQLite compiled to WebAssembly with the FTS5 index; build an inverted index (term → packages) at export time; scan an array of records."
msgstr "**选项。** 携带编译为 WebAssembly 的 SQLite 及其 FTS5 索引；在导出时构建倒排索引（词 → 包）；扫描记录数组。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:157
msgid "**Choice.** A linear scan. The registry has a few thousand packages, so one query touches a few thousand short records, which is cheap for a worker. Substring matching (`pars` finds `parser`) and numeric filters need no tokenizer and no posting lists, and the index stays a plain JSON file that the export script writes in a few lines. A WebAssembly database would add a large download to every visit."
msgstr "**选择。** 线性扫描。注册表只有几千个包，所以一次查询只涉及几千条短记录，对 worker 来说开销很小。子串匹配（`pars` 能找到 `parser`）和数值过滤不需要分词器和倒排表，索引也保持为一个导出脚本几行代码就能写出的普通 JSON 文件。WebAssembly 数据库会给每次访问增加大量下载。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:163
msgid "Run the search in a Web Worker"
msgstr "在 Web Worker 中运行搜索"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:165
msgid "**Problem.** Parsing the whole index and sorting it on the main thread would block rendering."
msgstr "**问题。** 在主线程上解析整个索引并排序会阻塞渲染。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:168
msgid "**Choice.** The worker loads `search-index.json` once and keeps the records in memory; queries are messages with an `id`, and each reply resolves the request with the same `id`, so concurrent queries cannot be confused. The URL carries `generated_at` from the manifest as a version parameter, and a new manifest terminates and restarts the worker, so a stale index is never mixed with new feeds."
msgstr "**选择。** worker 只加载一次 `search-index.json` 并把记录保存在内存中；查询是带 `id` 的消息，每个回复都只解决具有相同 `id` 的请求，因此并发查询不会混淆。URL 以清单中的 `generated_at` 作为版本参数，新的清单会终止并重启 worker，因此过期的索引永远不会与新的 feed 混用。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:174
msgid "Normalise once, at export"
msgstr "导出时一次性规范化"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:176
msgid "**Problem.** Case-insensitive matching needs lower-cased text on both sides."
msgstr "**问题。** 不区分大小写的匹配需要两边都是小写文本。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:178
msgid "**Choice.** Python lower-cases the records at export (`str.strip().lower()`); the worker lower-cases only the needle (`trim().toLowerCase()`). Both apply the Unicode default case mapping, so for ordinary package metadata the two sides agree. The MoonBit `normalize_text` implements the lower-casing step through the same JavaScript function, so that MoonBit code compiled for the static site normalises text exactly as the worker does."
msgstr "**选择。** Python 在导出时把记录转为小写（`str.strip().lower()`）；worker 只把查询词转为小写（`trim().toLowerCase()`）。两者都使用 Unicode 默认大小写映射，因此对于普通的包元数据，两边结果一致。MoonBit 的 `normalize_text` 通过同一个 JavaScript 函数实现转小写这一步，使为静态站点编译的 MoonBit 代码与 worker 的规范化方式完全相同。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:185
msgid "Keep the version tag in MoonBit"
msgstr "把版本标记放在 MoonBit 中"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:187
msgid "`runtime_version` gives the compiled JavaScript module a fixed identity. The static build (`scripts/build_static_site.mjs`) compiles the package before `next build`, so a MoonBit change that breaks the module stops the static build."
msgstr "`runtime_version` 为编译后的 JavaScript 模块提供固定标识。静态构建（`scripts/build_static_site.mjs`）在 `next build` 之前编译该包，因此破坏该模块的 MoonBit 修改会让静态构建失败。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:194
msgid "Agreement with the dynamic site"
msgstr "与动态站点的一致性"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:196
msgid "The worker and the server decode `ast` and `expr` with the same functions from `lib/query.ts`, so a query means the same formula in both modes. The term semantics differ on purpose:"
msgstr "worker 和服务器使用 `lib/query.ts` 中相同的函数解码 `ast` 和 `expr`，因此一个查询在两种模式下表示同一个公式。项的语义则有意不同："

#: manual/design/static_search.md:200
msgid "Text terms (`text`, `owner`, `package`, `keyword`, `description`) are substring tests in the static site, so `pars` also finds `sparse`. The server sends them to SQLite FTS5, which matches token prefixes (`pars*`). `license` and `repository` are substring tests in both modes."
msgstr "文本项（`text`、`owner`、`package`、`keyword`、`description`）在静态站点中是子串测试，所以 `pars` 也会找到 `sparse`。服务器则把它们交给 SQLite FTS5，后者匹配词元前缀（`pars*`）。`license` 和 `repository` 在两种模式下都是子串测试。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:204
msgid "The server rejects a term whose operator does not fit its field (for example `rank>=A`) with HTTP 400; the worker evaluates it anyway, using equality for labels and numbers and a substring test for text."
msgstr "服务器会以 HTTP 400 拒绝运算符与字段不匹配的项（例如 `rank>=A`）；worker 则照常求值，对标签和数字使用相等比较，对文本使用子串测试。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:207
msgid "With a query and no explicit sort, the static site orders by the coordination count above. The server orders AST queries by score and ranks legacy text queries by FTS5 `bm25`."
msgstr "有查询且未显式指定排序时，静态站点按上述协调计数排序。服务器则按分数排列 AST 查询，并用 FTS5 `bm25` 为旧式文本查询排序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:210
msgid "Rank and momentum values must match the label exactly in the static site (`rank=s` matches nothing). The server accepts them in any case and rejects unknown labels with HTTP 400."
msgstr "在静态站点中，等级和势头的值必须与标签完全一致（`rank=s` 匹配不到任何结果）。服务器不区分大小写地接受它们，并对未知标签返回 HTTP 400。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:213
msgid "An empty numeric value compares with $0$ in the static site; the server rejects it with HTTP 400."
msgstr "在静态站点中，空的数值与 $0$ 比较；服务器则以 HTTP 400 拒绝。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:215
msgid "`updated` sorts by year in the static site and by the full timestamp on the server."
msgstr "`updated` 在静态站点中按年份排序，在服务器上按完整时间戳排序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:217
msgid "Ties in a descending static sort are broken by name descending. The server breaks ties by name ascending, after score descending for the `growth`, `downloads`, `dependents` and `recent` sorts."
msgstr "静态站点的降序排序中，并列项按名称降序打破。服务器按名称升序打破并列；对 `growth`、`downloads`、`dependents` 和 `recent` 排序，则先按分数降序。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:220
msgid "The server returns at most `limit` results (20 by default, at most 100); the static site returns every match."
msgstr "服务器最多返回 `limit` 个结果（默认 20，最多 100）；静态站点返回所有匹配。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:223
msgid "Complexity"
msgstr "复杂度"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:225
msgid "Let $N$ be the number of records, $L$ the number of term leaves of the query and $\\ell$ the length of the longest normalised field. One term test costs $O(\\ell)$ for numeric and label terms and at most $O(\\ell\\,|v|)$ for a substring test. Then"
msgstr "设 $N$ 为记录数，$L$ 为查询的项叶子数，$\\ell$ 为最长规范化字段的长度。一次项测试对数值和标签项的代价为 $O(\\ell)$，对子串测试至多为 $O(\\ell\\,|v|)$。于是"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:238
msgid "A comparison costs $O(1)$ for the key sorts but $O(L \\ell |v|)$ for relevance, because the comparator recomputes $\\operatorname{rel}$ for both records instead of caching it. Relevance sorting is therefore $O(N \\log N \\cdot L \\ell |v|)$, a factor of $\\log N$ more term tests than the filter. Memory is $O(N F \\ell)$ for the resident index. All results are returned; there is no limit in static mode."
msgstr "对键排序而言，一次比较的代价为 $O(1)$；对相关度排序则为 $O(L \\ell |v|)$，因为比较器每次都为两条记录重新计算 $\\operatorname{rel}$ 而不缓存。因此相关度排序为 $O(N \\log N \\cdot L \\ell |v|)$，项测试次数比过滤多出 $\\log N$ 倍。常驻索引的内存为 $O(N F \\ell)$。所有结果都会返回；静态模式没有数量限制。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:247
msgid "**SQLite in WebAssembly** would make static and dynamic results identical but costs a large download and a WebAssembly runtime on every visit."
msgstr "**WebAssembly 中的 SQLite** 能让静态和动态结果完全一致，但每次访问都要付出大量下载和一个 WebAssembly 运行时的代价。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:249
msgid "**A client-side full-text library** (inverted index with tf–idf or BM25) would rank better for free text but needs a tokenizer that agrees with the FTS5 tokenizer to be consistent, and loses substring matching."
msgstr "**客户端全文检索库**（带 tf–idf 或 BM25 的倒排索引）对自由文本的排序会更好，但为保持一致需要一个与 FTS5 分词器一致的分词器，而且会失去子串匹配。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:252
msgid "**Splitting the index per owner or per letter** would shrink the first download but make OR queries across shards fetch many files."
msgstr "**按所有者或首字母拆分索引**可以减小首次下载量，但会让跨分片的 OR 查询需要获取许多文件。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:257
msgid "The static search does not tokenise, stem or rank by text statistics, and it does not correct spelling."
msgstr "静态搜索不分词、不做词干提取、不按文本统计量排序，也不做拼写纠正。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:259
msgid "It returns every match; paging and limits are left to the interface."
msgstr "它返回所有匹配项；分页和数量限制留给界面处理。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:260
msgid "The MoonBit package does not implement the index or the query evaluation; those are in Python and TypeScript."
msgstr "MoonBit 包不实现索引或查询求值；它们位于 Python 和 TypeScript 中。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:262
msgid "In this release the worker does not import the MoonBit module; its TypeScript normalisation additionally trims the needle, which `normalize_text` does not."
msgstr "在此版本中，worker 并不导入 MoonBit 模块；它的 TypeScript 规范化还会去除查询词的首尾空白，而 `normalize_text` 不会。"

#: manual/design/static_search.md:265
msgid "The data is as fresh as the last export; there is no incremental update."
msgstr "数据的新鲜度取决于最近一次导出；没有增量更新。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:1
